  "fields": [
    {
      "entryId": "act-28-26",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Paul closes Acts with Isaiah 6 over the Jews in Rome: hearing, not perceiving — and turns to the Gentiles, who will hear. First principle: the book that opened with Israel ends with the light going to the nations, exactly as written.",
      "density": 2.3643,
      "words": 42,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 23,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-15-16",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "James settles the Gentile question with Amos: God returns and rebuilds David's fallen booth so the residue of men may seek the Lord. First principle: Gentile inclusion is not a plan B — it is the rebuilt tabernacle, prophesied.",
      "density": 2.2893,
      "words": 39,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 23,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-4-26",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The church prays Psalm 2 over the threats of rulers: kings stood up, rulers gathered — against the Lord and His Christ. First principle: opposition to the gospel is the prophesied rage of kings; the heavens answer with boldness, not retreat.",
      "density": 2.2821,
      "words": 41,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-7-49",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Stephen closes with Isaiah 66: the Most High dwells not in temples made with hands. First principle: God cannot be housed — the accusation against the temple is that its makers trusted the building, not the Presence.",
      "density": 2.1821,
      "words": 37,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-1-11",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The angels fix the ascension as the pattern of return: this same Jesus shall so come in like manner. First principle: the clouds that received Him are the clouds that will bring Him — Zechariah 14's Olivet schedule holds.",
      "density": 2.1179,
      "words": 39,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-2-17",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Peter opens Joel 2 at Pentecost: sons and daughters prophesy, young men see visions. First principle: the last days begin at the cross and the Spirit — the prophecy Peter quotes is still running.",
      "density": 1.9929,
      "words": 34,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-13-47",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Paul and Barnabas quote Isaiah 49 as their commission to turn to the Gentiles. First principle: the Servant's worldwide salvation is carried forward by His witnesses — ordained for eternal life, not an afterthought.",
      "density": 1.9929,
      "words": 34,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-8-32",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The Ethiopian eunuch reads Isaiah 53; Philip preaches Jesus from that very text. First principle: Isaiah 53 is the key that opens the Old Testament — and Philip uses it for personal evangelism.",
      "density": 1.9679,
      "words": 33,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-7-37",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Stephen quotes Deuteronomy 18 and applies it: the Prophet God would raise up has come. First principle: Deuteronomy 18 is a messianic office, and refusing to hear Him is the judgment it warns of.",
      "density": 1.9357,
      "words": 34,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-17-31",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "God has fixed a day and a Judge, giving assurance to all by raising Him from the dead. First principle: the resurrection is the receipt of future judgment — the ordained Man will judge in righteousness.",
      "density": 1.9286,
      "words": 36,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-4-11",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Peter, standing in the Sanhedrin, quotes the Stone psalm against the builders themselves. First principle: salvation is in no other name — the Stone you rejected is the only foundation God laid.",
      "density": 1.8857,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-10-43",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Peter's summary to Cornelius: all the prophets witness that through Christ's name whosoever believeth receives remission of sins. First principle: the prophetic corpus has one subject and one offer — forgiveness through the Name.",
      "density": 1.8786,
      "words": 34,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-7-50",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The Maker of all needs no house of stone. First principle: creation precedes temple; the God whose hand made everything cannot be contained by anything His hand has made.",
      "density": 1.8679,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-1-8",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Power from the Holy Ghost sends witnesses from Jerusalem to the ends of the earth. First principle: Isaiah 49's salvation-to-the-ends becomes the church's marching order — the Spirit is the engine of prophecy.",
      "density": 1.8536,
      "words": 33,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-7-32",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "At the bush, God names Himself the God of the patriarchs — and Moses trembles. First principle: the covenant God binds Himself to generations; the resurrection hope is folded into His very self-identification.",
      "density": 1.8536,
      "words": 33,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-3-18",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The sufferings of Christ were shewn by all the prophets beforehand — and God hath so fulfilled them. First principle: the cross is God's foretold plan, executed on schedule through guilty hands.",
      "density": 1.8286,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-2-34",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Peter argues from Psalm 110: David did not ascend, yet spoke of enthronement — fulfilled in Jesus. First principle: the prophecy outruns its author; the Lord at God's right hand is David's Son.",
      "density": 1.7964,
      "words": 33,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 17,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-3-25",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Peter preaches to Israel as children of the covenant — Abraham's seed blessing all kindreds. First principle: the gospel to Jerusalem is Genesis 12 arriving on schedule, first to the covenant family.",
      "density": 1.7714,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 17,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-7-3",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Stephen recounts the call of Abraham: leave kindred, come into the land I shew thee. First principle: the covenant story begins with a departure on promise — faith walks before it sees.",
      "density": 1.7714,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 17,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-1-20",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Psalm 69 and 109 govern the choice of a twelfth witness — habitation desolate, another takes his office. First principle: the apostles resolve even church order by written prophecy.",
      "density": 1.7536,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-7-7",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "God tells Abraham of bondage, judgment, and a fourth-generation exodus. First principle: prophecy names the oppression and its end before either exists — and God keeps the calendar.",
      "density": 1.7286,
      "words": 28,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-13-33",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Paul reads Psalm 2 of the resurrection: God fulfilled the promise by raising Jesus. First principle: the resurrection is the enthronement decree — begotten again, as firstborn from the dead.",
      "density": 1.6643,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 16,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-13-34",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Isaiah 55's sure mercies are read of the Holy One who sees no corruption. First principle: the covenant mercies promised to David are delivered as an incorruptible, risen Savior.",
      "density": 1.5821,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 15,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-3-22",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Moses said: A prophet shall the Lord your God raise up… like unto me. Textual proof: Deuteronomy 18:15-19 quoted as fulfilled in Jesus; same text as John 1:45.",
      "density": 1.5,
      "words": 28,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 14,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": [
          "Deuteronomy 18:15",
          "John 1:45"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-2-25",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Peter quotes Psalm 16:8-11 for Jesus' resurrection. Textual proof: Acts 2:25-36 argues David did not rise; his Son did. Paul makes the same argument in Acts 13:35-37.",
      "density": 1.3607,
      "words": 27,
      "sentences": 3,
      "maxSentenceWords": 12,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": [
          "Acts 2:25",
          "Acts 13:35"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "act-1-16",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Peter reads Judas's betrayal from David's own words. First principle: even treachery inside the Twelve moved along rails Scripture had already laid.",
      "density": 1.35,
      "words": 22,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 14,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
